{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pv2gBRxELSJ2mp1pYW9ACq","type":"tool_result","content":"# microtags\n\n[![tests](https://img.shields.io/github/actions/workflow/status/nichoth/microtags/nodejs.yml?style=flat-square)](https://github.com/nichoth/microtags/actions/workflows/nodejs.yml)\n[![types](https://img.shields.io/npm/types/microtags?style=flat-square)](README.md)\n[![module](https://img.shields.io/badge/module-ESM%2FCJS-blue?style=flat-square)](README.md)\n[![semantic versioning](https://img.shields.io/badge/semver-2.0.0-blue?logo=semver&style=flat-square)](https://semver.org/)\n[![Common Changelog](https://nichoth.github.io/badge/common-changelog.svg)](./CHANGELOG.md)\n[![install size](https://flat.badgen.net/packagephobia/install/microtags?cache-control=no-cache)](https://packagephobia.com/result?p=microtags)\n[![gzip size](https://img.shields.io/bundlephobia/minzip/microtags?style=flat-square)](https://bundlephobia.com/package/microtags)\n[![license](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Big_Time-blue?style=flat-square)](LICENSE)\n\nWeb component helper with reactive props, automatic cleanup, and\n[no Shadow DOM](https://gomakethings.com/the-shadow-dom-is-an-antipattern/).\nReactive via [`alien-signals`](https://github.com/stackblitz/alien-signals),\ninspired by [`nanotags`](https://github.com/psd-coder/nanotags).\n\nThis package adds some provisions for serverside rendering.\n\n| Entry | Size (min + brotli) |\n|-------|---------------------|\n| `microtags` | <!-- size -->4.01 KB<!-- /size --> |\n| `microtags/htm` | <!-- size:htm -->1.23 KB<!-- /size:htm --> |\n\n<details><summary><h2>Contents</h2></summary>\n\n<!-- toc -->\n\n- [Install](#install)\n  * [Import map](#import-map)\n  * [Pre-bundled](#pre-bundled)\n- [Get Started](#get-started)\n  * [1. Call `.define`](#1-call-define)\n  * [2. Call the `.with*` Methods](#2-call-the-with-methods)\n  * [3. Call `.setup`](#3-call-setup)\n- [Full Example](#full-example)\n- [Validation](#validation)\n  * [Prop validation](#prop-validation)\n    + [`p.schema` vs Standard Schema](#pschema-vs-standard-schema)\n  * [Client-side validation](#client-side-validation)\n- [Serverside Example](#serverside-example)\n  * [`.TAG`](#tag)\n  * [`.refs`](#refs)\n- [Hydration](#hydration)\n- [API](#api)\n  * [`define`](#define)\n    + [`ComponentBuilder`](#componentbuilder)\n  * [`builder.withProps`](#builderwithprops)\n    + [`p.json`](#pjson)\n    + [`p.schema`](#pschema)\n  * [`builder.withRefs(fn)`](#builderwithrefsfn)\n  * [`builder.withContexts`](#builderwithcontexts)\n    + [`.withContexts` Example](#withcontexts-example)\n  * [`builder.render(fn, options?)`](#builderrenderfn-options)\n  * [`builder.setup(ctx)`](#buildersetupctx)\n    + [`ctx`](#ctx)\n      - [`ctx` Methods](#ctx-methods)\n      - [`ctx.bind`](#ctxbind)\n  * [`bindProp`](#bindprop)\n- [Missing refs](#missing-refs)\n  * [Checking refs in tests](#checking-refs-in-tests)\n- [Typed Events](#typed-events)\n- [Templates](#templates)\n- [Subpath Exports](#subpath-exports)\n  * [`microtags/context`](#microtagscontext)\n  * [`microtags/render`](#microtagsrender)\n    + [`renderList`](#renderlist)\n      - [`renderList` Example](#renderlist-example)\n    + [`render`](#render)\n      - [`render` Example](#render-example)\n  * [`microtags/util`](#microtagsutil)\n    + [Coercion](#coercion)\n    + [`runAll`](#runall)\n    + [`toAttributes`](#toattributes)\n  * [`microtags/htm`](#microtagshtm)\n    + [What escaping does not cover](#what-escaping-does-not-cover)\n  * [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support)\n  * [`microtags/build`](#microtagsbuild)\n  * [`microtags/esbuild`](#microtagsesbuild)\n  * [`microtags/vite`](#microtagsvite)\n  * [`microbuild`](#microbuild)\n  * [`client:true` vs `--keep`](#clienttrue-vs---keep)\n- [Differences from `nanotags`](#differences-from-nanotags)\n  * [Reactivity primitive](#reactivity-primitive)\n  * [Effects + Subscriptions](#effects--subscriptions)\n  * [Refs: `r.all` instead of `r.many`](#refs-rall-instead-of-rmany)\n  * [Context API](#context-api)\n  * [Props](#props)\n  * [Not ported](#not-ported)\n  * [Additions / New Features](#additions--new-features)\n\n<!-- tocstop -->\n\n</details>\n\n## Install\n *\n * @param {Attrs} attrs An object for the attributes.\n * @returns {string} A string suitable for use as HTML attributes.\n */\nfunction toAttributes (attrs:Attrs):string\n```\n\n### `microtags/htm`\n\nA tagged-template string renderer that will expand any microtags\ninstances if finds. Exports `html`, `h`, `raw`, and the `Markup` type.\n`html`, `h`, and `raw` return `Markup`, not a string. Convert it with\n`String(m)` where a string is required, for example `innerHTML`. In the\nbrowser the same import resolves to a build that also exports `mount`;\nsee [ADR-007](./docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md).\n\n```ts\nimport { html, raw } from 'microtags/htm'\nimport { MyCounter } from './components.js'\n\nconst page = html`<div>\n    <${MyCounter} start=${5}>\n        <p>Extra children</p>\n    </${MyCounter}>\n    ${raw('<b>trusted markup</b>')}\n</div>`\n```\n\nWhen `html` meets a microtags element class, it splits props from\npassthrough attributes using the class's static `props` list, joins\nchildren into one string, and calls the static `render`. Plain string\ntag names emit ordinary HTML.\n\n**Escaping.** Every interpolated string is escaped (`<`, `>`, `&`, `\"`,\n`'`) before the parser sees it. Component output and `raw()` output\nare trusted and never re-escaped. Static template text is trusted.\n\n**Arrays.** Array children (from `.map()`) are flattened automatically.\n\n**Void elements.** Write void tags in the self-closing form, like\n`<br />`, `<img src=\"x\" />`, and `<input value=${v} />`. The output has\nno closing tag and no trailing slash, eg `<br>`. The `htm` parser does\nnot know which tags are void, so an unclosed `<br>` would be treated\nas an open tag and swallow the content after it. Instead of dropping\nthat content, the templater throws, on the server and in the browser,\nand the error names the tag and its self-closing form.\n\n**Custom elements.** A component tag always gets a closing tag in the\noutput, eg `<my-counter start=\"5\">...</my-counter>`, because HTML has no\nself-closing custom elements. In a template, close a component with\n`</${MyComponent}>` or with the `htm` shorthand `<//>`, which closes\nthe nearest open tag without repeating its name.\n\n#### What escaping does not cover\n\nEscaping keeps an interpolated string from becoming markup. It does not\nmake every value safe in every place it can go.\n\n**URL schemes.** Attribute escaping keeps a value inside its quotes,\nbut `href=${url}` with `url` set to `javascript:alert(1)` is still a\nworking link. The same goes for `src`, `action`, `formaction`, and\nother attributes that take a URL. Check the scheme yourself (for\nexample, allow only `http:`, `https:` and `mailto:`) before a URL from\nuser data reaches the template.\n\n**`<script>` and `<style>`.** HTML escaping is the wrong encoding inside\nthese elements. The browser does not decode entities there, so an\nescaped value comes out mangled, and HTML escaping does not stop a\nvalue from breaking out of a JavaScript string or a CSS rule. Do not\ninterpolate user data into them. To pass data to a script, serialize it\nas JSON in a `<script type=\"application/json\">` and escape `<` in the\nJSON, the way the hydration example's state script does.\n\n**`raw`.** `raw()` skips escaping by construction. Pass it only markup\nyou wrote or trust, never user data.\n\n**Attribute names.** Escaping covers values, not names. A name must\nstart with a letter, `_` or `:`, followed by letters, digits, `-`,\n`_`, `:` or `.`. Any other name, for example a key from a spread of\nuser data such as `x\" onload=\"...`, is skipped without an error, on the\nserver, in the browser, and on a component's host tag. Valid keys in the\nsame spread are still written.\n\n**Void elements.** A void element with children throws instead of\nrendering, on the server and in the browser. Write void tags in the\nself-closing form, `<input />`, so an unclosed tag cannot swallow the\nmarkup after it.\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/render-support`\n\nThe host-tag builder, prop serializers and attribute escaping that a\ncomponent's static `render` and `renderParts` use. Import it for its\nside effect:\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\n```\n\nIt is separate from core so that a client bundle with every\n`.render` link stripped leaves this code out. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater imports it already, and the [`microtags/build`](#microtagsbuild)\ntransform adds it to any module where it keeps a `.render` link, so\nonly code that calls a `render` or `renderParts` static without\neither needs this import. See\n[ADR-009](./docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md).\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\nNode-only. Strips [`.render()`](#builderrenderfn-options) calls from\ndefine chains so the client bundle contains only hydration code.\nRequires `typescript` as a peer dependency.\n\n```ts\nimport { transform } from 'microtags/build'\n\nconst result = transform(source, {\n    keep: ['my-notice'],   // keep these tags' render in the bundle\n    cascade: true,         // dead-import removal, default false\n    filename: 'app.ts',    // shown in warnings\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.code)\nfor (const w of result.warnings) {\n    console.warn(`${w.file}:${w.line} ${w.message}`)\n}\n```\n\n**Strip rule:** a `.render(...)` call is removed when it is a link in a\ncall chain rooted at a `define(...)` call imported from `microtags`,\nwith import aliases tracked. Nothing else named `render` is touched.\n\n**Keep rule (union):** the call is kept when its options argument is an\nobject literal containing `client: true`, or when the string literal\npassed to `define` is listed in `keep`.\n\n**Output fidelity:** removed spans are replaced with the same number of\nnewlines. Every other byte is unchanged, apart from the support import\nbelow. TS in, TS out.\n\n**Support import:** when a module keeps at least one `.render` link,\nthe transform appends `import 'microtags/render-support'` after the\nlast line, unless the module already imports it, so kept components\ncan render in the browser. A module where every link was stripped gets\nno such import, and a bundle with no kept link and no templater import\ncontains none of the server render code. A bundler config that aliases\n`microtags` to source should alias `microtags/render-support` too.\n\n**Unsupported:** `const b = define('x'); b.render(fn)` -- the\nnon-chained form is not matched and is left unchanged.\n\n**`client: true` detection:** only an object literal is recognised. A\nvariable or spread in the options position is not.\n\n**Type gap:** `MicrotagElementClass` declares `render` and `props` as\nalways present. After stripping, `render` is `undefined` at runtime.\n\n**Warnings** (each with file and line):\n\n| Kind | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `outside-chain` | `.render(` call not in a define chain |\n| `stripped-static` | `X.render(` after X's render was stripped |\n| `non-literal-tag` | `define(variable)` with `keep` set |\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/esbuild`\n\nNode-only esbuild plugin that calls [`transform`](#microtagsbuild) on\nevery matching file during the build.\n\n```ts\nimport { microtags } from 'microtags/esbuild'\n\n// in your esbuild config\nplugins: [\n    microtags({\n        cascade: true,\n        keep: ['my-notice'],\n    }),\n]\n```\n\nThe plugin accepts the same options as `transform` plus a file `filter`.\nWarnings are forwarded to esbuild's warning channel.\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/vite`\n\nNode-only Vite plugin, same interface as the\n[esbuild plugin](#microtagsesbuild).\n\n```ts\nimport { microtags } from 'microtags/vite'\n\n// in vite.config.ts\nplugins: [\n    microtags({\n        cascade: true,\n        keep: ['my-notice'],\n    }),\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### `microbuild`\n\nCLI for stripping `.render()` calls outside a bundler.\n\n```sh\n# stdin/stdout -- one file\ncat src/counter.ts | microbuild --cascade > dist/counter.ts\n\n# glob mode -- requires --outdir\nmicrobuild 'src/**/*.ts' --outdir dist --cascade --keep my-notice\n```\n\n`--keep` is repeatable and accepts comma-separated tag names. `--root`\nsets the base for output paths (defaults to the current directory).\nFiles are never rewritten in place.\n\nstdin mode transforms one file only. A multi-file app should use the\n[esbuild](#microtagsesbuild) or [vite](#microtagsvite) plugin, or\nglob mode.\n\n---\n\n### `client:true` vs `--keep`\n\nBoth prevent [`microbuild`](#microbuild) from stripping a component's\n`.render()` call, but they work at different levels:\n\n- **`{ client: true }`** is set in source, in the `.render()` options.\n  Use it for components that must render themselves in the browser --\n  for example, a notice inserted dynamically after page load. The\n  decision travels with the component and applies in every build.\n\n- **`--keep tag-name`** (or the `keep` option in the plugin) is set at\n  build time. Use it to override stripping for specific tags without\n  changing source, for example during development or in a build\n  variant that needs client rendering.\n\nBoth can be combined. A component is kept when either condition is met\n(union semantics).\n\n---\n\n## Differences from `nanotags`\n\n### Reactivity primitive\n\n`nanotags` uses `nanostores` atoms; `microtags` uses `alien-signals`.\n\n| nanotags (nanostores) | microtags (alien-signals) |\n|---|---|\n// Types and prop mapping shared by both builds of `microtags/preact`\n// (the default server build and the browser build). Never imports\n// render support. See ADR-010.\nimport type { FunctionComponent } from 'preact'\nimport type { RenderParts } from './builders.js'\n\n/**\n * The part of a microtags element class the adapter reads. Any class\n * from `setup` fits; `renderParts` is absent at runtime when the class\n * has no render link.\n */\nexport interface PreactElementClass<P = any> {\n    readonly TAG:string\n    readonly props:readonly string[]\n    readonly renderParts?:(\n        props:P,\n        options?:{ children?:string; attrs?:Record<string, string> }\n    ) => RenderParts\n}\n\n/** Map from callback prop name to DOM event name. */\nexport type EventMap = Record<string, string>\n\nexport interface ToPreactOptions<E extends EventMap = EventMap> {\n    /** e.g. `{ onChange: 'number-input:change' }` */\n    events?:E\n}\n\ntype AttrValue = string | number | boolean | null | undefined\n\n/** Host attributes passed through to the host tag. */\nexport interface PassthroughProps {\n    class?:string\n    id?:string\n    [aria:`aria-${string}`]:AttrValue\n    [data:`data-${string}`]:AttrValue\n}\n\n/** The declared props of an element class, all optional. */\nexport type DeclaredProps<C> =\n    C extends { renderParts?:(props:infer P, ...a:any[]) => any } ?\n        Partial<P> :\n        never\n\n/**\n * Props of the Preact component `toPreact` returns: the declared\n * props, one callback per mapped event, passthrough host attributes,\n * and no children.\n */\nexport type PreactProps<C, E extends EventMap = Record<never, never>> =\n    DeclaredProps<C> &\n    { [K in keyof E]?:(ev:CustomEvent) => void } &\n    PassthroughProps &\n    { children?:never }\n\nexport type PreactComponent<C, E extends EventMap> =\n    FunctionComponent<PreactProps<C, E>>\n\n/** Props split by where they go on the host. */\nexport interface SplitProps {\n    /** declared props, by name */\n    own:Record<string, unknown>\n    /** handlers, by DOM event name */\n    on:Record<string, unknown>\n    /** passthrough host attributes */\n    rest:Record<string, unknown>\n}\n\n/**\n * Split adapter props into declared props, event handlers (keyed by DOM\n * event name) and passthrough attributes. Throws, naming the tag, when\n * children are passed.\n */\nexport function splitProps (\n    El:PreactElementClass,\n    events:EventMap,\n    props:Record<string, unknown>\n):SplitProps {\n    if (props.children !== undefined) {\n        throw new Error(`microtags/preact: <${El.TAG}> takes no children`)\n    }\n    const own:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n    const on:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n    const rest:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n    for (const k in props) {\n        if (k === 'children') continue\n        if (El.props.includes(k)) own[k] = props[k]\n        else if (Object.hasOwn(events, k)) on[events[k]] = props[k]\n        else rest[k] = props[k]\n    }\n    return { own, on, rest }\n}\n// `microtags/preact`, browser build. Renders the host tag only: the\n// declared props go to the host's prop accessors, mapped events become\n// `on<event-name>` listeners, and a fixed empty `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n// keeps Preact out of the host's children. Never imports render\n// support. See ADR-010.\nimport { h, type VNode } from 'preact'\nimport {\n    splitProps,\n    type EventMap,\n    type PreactComponent,\n    type PreactElementClass,\n    type ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\nexport type {\n    DeclaredProps,\n    EventMap,\n    PassthroughProps,\n    PreactComponent,\n    PreactElementClass,\n    PreactProps,\n    ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\n// One shared value: Preact writes `innerHTML` only when `__html`\n// changes, and never while hydrating.\nconst EMPTY = { __html: '' }\n\n/**\n * Wrap a microtags element class as a Preact component. Preact owns the\n * host and its attributes; the element owns the host's children.\n */\nexport function toPreact<\n    C extends PreactElementClass,\n    E extends EventMap = Record<never, never>,\n> (El:C, options?:ToPreactOptions<E>):PreactComponent<C, E> {\n    const events:EventMap = options?.events ?? {}\n    return (props:Record<string, unknown>):VNode<any> => {\n        const { own, on, rest } = splitProps(El, events, props)\n        const vprops:Record<string, unknown> = { ...rest, ...own }\n        for (const k in on) vprops['on' + k] = on[k]\n        vprops.dangerouslySetInnerHTML = EMPTY\n        return h(El.TAG, vprops)\n    }\n}\n# ADR-010: Preact owns the host, the element owns its children\n\n**Date:** 2026-11-08\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size), [ADR-005][adr-005] and\n[ADR-009][adr-009] (render links and render support)\n\n## Context\n\n`../components` (`@substrate-system/components`) is moving its\ncomponents onto microtags, and they have to work inside Preact apps.\nThat covers a client-only Preact render and a Preact `hydrate` of a\nserver-rendered page. A microtags element placed in a Preact tree\nfails in both server cases.\n\nOn the server, Preact's `renderToString` emits an empty host, such as\n`<number-input min=\"1\"></number-input>`. Preact only knows the host\ntag. It does not know that the component has markup of its own, so\nthe page arrives without the component's input or buttons.\n\nIn the browser, Preact 10's `hydrate` collects every existing child of\nan element it hydrates and removes each child it has no vnode for. The\ncomponent's own markup has no vnode, so even if the server sent it,\n`hydrate` deletes it. The only exception is an element whose vnode has\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Preact leaves that element's children alone.\n\nThe terms below have their `CONTEXT.md` meanings. **Hydration** is the\nintent: attaching behaviour to markup that already exists in the\ndocument. **Adopt** is the mechanism: walking markup against existing\nDOM and binding to it without creating nodes. A microtags element\nhydrates itself when its class is registered. The adapter's job is to\nkeep Preact from undoing that hydration. It does not adopt anything\nitself.\n\n## Decision\n\nAdd a `microtags/preact` entry that exports `toPreact(El, options?)`.\nIt returns a Preact component that renders the element's host tag.\nOwnership is split at the host:\n\n- Preact owns the host tag and its attributes.\n- The element owns the host's children.\n\n**On the server**, the adapter builds the host vnode from the\ncomponent's render parts (the `renderParts` static, ADR-009's render\nsupport behind a new registry key). The attributes come from the\nparts' `attrs`, and the parts' `html` goes in through\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. `renderToString` then produces the same\nmarkup as the component's own `render` static. A class whose render\nlink was stripped has no `renderParts`, so the adapter throws an error\nthat names the tag.\n\n**In the browser**, the adapter gives the host one shared, fixed\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` whose `__html` is the empty string. It also\npasses the declared props as vnode props, which Preact assigns as\nproperties because the host defines an accessor for each one. Mapped\nevents are passed as `on<event-name>` props. The mechanism depends on\ntwo branches of Preact's element diff:\n\n1. While hydrating, Preact neither writes `innerHTML` nor removes the\n   element's existing children. The server markup stays and the\n   element adopts it.\n2. Outside hydration, Preact writes `innerHTML` only when the new\n   `__html` differs from the old one. The value never changes, so it\n   is written at most once, on the first non-hydrating render. On a\n   client-only mount that write empties the host once, and the element\n   renders itself when it connects. Later renders never touch the\n   children.\n\nBoth branches were verified in Preact 10.29.7. The `preact` dev\ndependency is pinned, so a Preact change arrives as a deliberate bump,\nand the browser tests (hydrate keeps inner nodes, re-render keeps\nthem, typed input survives) check it.\n\nThe browser build is selected by a `browser` export condition, as\n`microtags/htm` already is, and never imports render support.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\nADR-001-alien-signals-for-reactivity.md\nADR-002-no-shadow-dom.md\nADR-003-standard-schema-for-prop-validation.md\nADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\nADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\nADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\nADR-007-client-templater.md\nADR-008-serialized-server-state.md\nADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md\nADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md\nINDEX.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd578c50-847c-417e-9dc9-883d9c7ecbfc","uuid":"970add55-1c36-4e52-8dad-e32f778528c7","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:22:06.243Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# microtags\n\n[![tests](https://img.shields.io/github/actions/workflow/status/nichoth/microtags/nodejs.yml?style=flat-square)](https://github.com/nichoth/microtags/actions/workflows/nodejs.yml)\n[![types](https://img.shields.io/npm/types/microtags?style=flat-square)](README.md)\n[![module](https://img.shields.io/badge/module-ESM%2FCJS-blue?style=flat-square)](README.md)\n[![semantic versioning](https://img.shields.io/badge/semver-2.0.0-blue?logo=semver&style=flat-square)](https://semver.org/)\n[![Common Changelog](https://nichoth.github.io/badge/common-changelog.svg)](./CHANGELOG.md)\n[![install size](https://flat.badgen.net/packagephobia/install/microtags?cache-control=no-cache)](https://packagephobia.com/result?p=microtags)\n[![gzip size](https://img.shields.io/bundlephobia/minzip/microtags?style=flat-square)](https://bundlephobia.com/package/microtags)\n[![license](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Big_Time-blue?style=flat-square)](LICENSE)\n\nWeb component helper with reactive props, automatic cleanup, and\n[no Shadow DOM](https://gomakethings.com/the-shadow-dom-is-an-antipattern/).\nReactive via [`alien-signals`](https://github.com/stackblitz/alien-signals),\ninspired by [`nanotags`](https://github.com/psd-coder/nanotags).\n\nThis package adds some provisions for serverside rendering.\n\n| Entry | Size (min + brotli) |\n|-------|---------------------|\n| `microtags` | <!-- size -->4.01 KB<!-- /size --> |\n| `microtags/htm` | <!-- size:htm -->1.23 KB<!-- /size:htm --> |\n\n<details><summary><h2>Contents</h2></summary>\n\n<!-- toc -->\n\n- [Install](#install)\n  * [Import map](#import-map)\n  * [Pre-bundled](#pre-bundled)\n- [Get Started](#get-started)\n  * [1. Call `.define`](#1-call-define)\n  * [2. Call the `.with*` Methods](#2-call-the-with-methods)\n  * [3. Call `.setup`](#3-call-setup)\n- [Full Example](#full-example)\n- [Validation](#validation)\n  * [Prop validation](#prop-validation)\n    + [`p.schema` vs Standard Schema](#pschema-vs-standard-schema)\n  * [Client-side validation](#client-side-validation)\n- [Serverside Example](#serverside-example)\n  * [`.TAG`](#tag)\n  * [`.refs`](#refs)\n- [Hydration](#hydration)\n- [API](#api)\n  * [`define`](#define)\n    + [`ComponentBuilder`](#componentbuilder)\n  * [`builder.withProps`](#builderwithprops)\n    + [`p.json`](#pjson)\n    + [`p.schema`](#pschema)\n  * [`builder.withRefs(fn)`](#builderwithrefsfn)\n  * [`builder.withContexts`](#builderwithcontexts)\n    + [`.withContexts` Example](#withcontexts-example)\n  * [`builder.render(fn, options?)`](#builderrenderfn-options)\n  * [`builder.setup(ctx)`](#buildersetupctx)\n    + [`ctx`](#ctx)\n      - [`ctx` Methods](#ctx-methods)\n      - [`ctx.bind`](#ctxbind)\n  * [`bindProp`](#bindprop)\n- [Missing refs](#missing-refs)\n  * [Checking refs in tests](#checking-refs-in-tests)\n- [Typed Events](#typed-events)\n- [Templates](#templates)\n- [Subpath Exports](#subpath-exports)\n  * [`microtags/context`](#microtagscontext)\n  * [`microtags/render`](#microtagsrender)\n    + [`renderList`](#renderlist)\n      - [`renderList` Example](#renderlist-example)\n    + [`render`](#render)\n      - [`render` Example](#render-example)\n  * [`microtags/util`](#microtagsutil)\n    + [Coercion](#coercion)\n    + [`runAll`](#runall)\n    + [`toAttributes`](#toattributes)\n  * [`microtags/htm`](#microtagshtm)\n    + [What escaping does not cover](#what-escaping-does-not-cover)\n  * [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support)\n  * [`microtags/build`](#microtagsbuild)\n  * [`microtags/esbuild`](#microtagsesbuild)\n  * [`microtags/vite`](#microtagsvite)\n  * [`microbuild`](#microbuild)\n  * [`client:true` vs `--keep`](#clienttrue-vs---keep)\n- [Differences from `nanotags`](#differences-from-nanotags)\n  * [Reactivity primitive](#reactivity-primitive)\n  * [Effects + Subscriptions](#effects--subscriptions)\n  * [Refs: `r.all` instead of `r.many`](#refs-rall-instead-of-rmany)\n  * [Context API](#context-api)\n  * [Props](#props)\n  * [Not ported](#not-ported)\n  * [Additions / New Features](#additions--new-features)\n\n<!-- tocstop -->\n\n</details>\n\n## Install\n *\n * @param {Attrs} attrs An object for the attributes.\n * @returns {string} A string suitable for use as HTML attributes.\n */\nfunction toAttributes (attrs:Attrs):string\n```\n\n### `microtags/htm`\n\nA tagged-template string renderer that will expand any microtags\ninstances if finds. Exports `html`, `h`, `raw`, and the `Markup` type.\n`html`, `h`, and `raw` return `Markup`, not a string. Convert it with\n`String(m)` where a string is required, for example `innerHTML`. In the\nbrowser the same import resolves to a build that also exports `mount`;\nsee [ADR-007](./docs/adr/ADR-007-client-templater.md).\n\n```ts\nimport { html, raw } from 'microtags/htm'\nimport { MyCounter } from './components.js'\n\nconst page = html`<div>\n    <${MyCounter} start=${5}>\n        <p>Extra children</p>\n    </${MyCounter}>\n    ${raw('<b>trusted markup</b>')}\n</div>`\n```\n\nWhen `html` meets a microtags element class, it splits props from\npassthrough attributes using the class's static `props` list, joins\nchildren into one string, and calls the static `render`. Plain string\ntag names emit ordinary HTML.\n\n**Escaping.** Every interpolated string is escaped (`<`, `>`, `&`, `\"`,\n`'`) before the parser sees it. Component output and `raw()` output\nare trusted and never re-escaped. Static template text is trusted.\n\n**Arrays.** Array children (from `.map()`) are flattened automatically.\n\n**Void elements.** Write void tags in the self-closing form, like\n`<br />`, `<img src=\"x\" />`, and `<input value=${v} />`. The output has\nno closing tag and no trailing slash, eg `<br>`. The `htm` parser does\nnot know which tags are void, so an unclosed `<br>` would be treated\nas an open tag and swallow the content after it. Instead of dropping\nthat content, the templater throws, on the server and in the browser,\nand the error names the tag and its self-closing form.\n\n**Custom elements.** A component tag always gets a closing tag in the\noutput, eg `<my-counter start=\"5\">...</my-counter>`, because HTML has no\nself-closing custom elements. In a template, close a component with\n`</${MyComponent}>` or with the `htm` shorthand `<//>`, which closes\nthe nearest open tag without repeating its name.\n\n#### What escaping does not cover\n\nEscaping keeps an interpolated string from becoming markup. It does not\nmake every value safe in every place it can go.\n\n**URL schemes.** Attribute escaping keeps a value inside its quotes,\nbut `href=${url}` with `url` set to `javascript:alert(1)` is still a\nworking link. The same goes for `src`, `action`, `formaction`, and\nother attributes that take a URL. Check the scheme yourself (for\nexample, allow only `http:`, `https:` and `mailto:`) before a URL from\nuser data reaches the template.\n\n**`<script>` and `<style>`.** HTML escaping is the wrong encoding inside\nthese elements. The browser does not decode entities there, so an\nescaped value comes out mangled, and HTML escaping does not stop a\nvalue from breaking out of a JavaScript string or a CSS rule. Do not\ninterpolate user data into them. To pass data to a script, serialize it\nas JSON in a `<script type=\"application/json\">` and escape `<` in the\nJSON, the way the hydration example's state script does.\n\n**`raw`.** `raw()` skips escaping by construction. Pass it only markup\nyou wrote or trust, never user data.\n\n**Attribute names.** Escaping covers values, not names. A name must\nstart with a letter, `_` or `:`, followed by letters, digits, `-`,\n`_`, `:` or `.`. Any other name, for example a key from a spread of\nuser data such as `x\" onload=\"...`, is skipped without an error, on the\nserver, in the browser, and on a component's host tag. Valid keys in the\nsame spread are still written.\n\n**Void elements.** A void element with children throws instead of\nrendering, on the server and in the browser. Write void tags in the\nself-closing form, `<input />`, so an unclosed tag cannot swallow the\nmarkup after it.\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/render-support`\n\nThe host-tag builder, prop serializers and attribute escaping that a\ncomponent's static `render` and `renderParts` use. Import it for its\nside effect:\n\n```ts\nimport 'microtags/render-support'\n```\n\nIt is separate from core so that a client bundle with every\n`.render` link stripped leaves this code out. The `microtags/htm`\ntemplater imports it already, and the [`microtags/build`](#microtagsbuild)\ntransform adds it to any module where it keeps a `.render` link, so\nonly code that calls a `render` or `renderParts` static without\neither needs this import. See\n[ADR-009](./docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md).\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/build`\n\nNode-only. Strips [`.render()`](#builderrenderfn-options) calls from\ndefine chains so the client bundle contains only hydration code.\nRequires `typescript` as a peer dependency.\n\n```ts\nimport { transform } from 'microtags/build'\n\nconst result = transform(source, {\n    keep: ['my-notice'],   // keep these tags' render in the bundle\n    cascade: true,         // dead-import removal, default false\n    filename: 'app.ts',    // shown in warnings\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.code)\nfor (const w of result.warnings) {\n    console.warn(`${w.file}:${w.line} ${w.message}`)\n}\n```\n\n**Strip rule:** a `.render(...)` call is removed when it is a link in a\ncall chain rooted at a `define(...)` call imported from `microtags`,\nwith import aliases tracked. Nothing else named `render` is touched.\n\n**Keep rule (union):** the call is kept when its options argument is an\nobject literal containing `client: true`, or when the string literal\npassed to `define` is listed in `keep`.\n\n**Output fidelity:** removed spans are replaced with the same number of\nnewlines. Every other byte is unchanged, apart from the support import\nbelow. TS in, TS out.\n\n**Support import:** when a module keeps at least one `.render` link,\nthe transform appends `import 'microtags/render-support'` after the\nlast line, unless the module already imports it, so kept components\ncan render in the browser. A module where every link was stripped gets\nno such import, and a bundle with no kept link and no templater import\ncontains none of the server render code. A bundler config that aliases\n`microtags` to source should alias `microtags/render-support` too.\n\n**Unsupported:** `const b = define('x'); b.render(fn)` -- the\nnon-chained form is not matched and is left unchanged.\n\n**`client: true` detection:** only an object literal is recognised. A\nvariable or spread in the options position is not.\n\n**Type gap:** `MicrotagElementClass` declares `render` and `props` as\nalways present. After stripping, `render` is `undefined` at runtime.\n\n**Warnings** (each with file and line):\n\n| Kind | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `outside-chain` | `.render(` call not in a define chain |\n| `stripped-static` | `X.render(` after X's render was stripped |\n| `non-literal-tag` | `define(variable)` with `keep` set |\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/esbuild`\n\nNode-only esbuild plugin that calls [`transform`](#microtagsbuild) on\nevery matching file during the build.\n\n```ts\nimport { microtags } from 'microtags/esbuild'\n\n// in your esbuild config\nplugins: [\n    microtags({\n        cascade: true,\n        keep: ['my-notice'],\n    }),\n]\n```\n\nThe plugin accepts the same options as `transform` plus a file `filter`.\nWarnings are forwarded to esbuild's warning channel.\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/vite`\n\nNode-only Vite plugin, same interface as the\n[esbuild plugin](#microtagsesbuild).\n\n```ts\nimport { microtags } from 'microtags/vite'\n\n// in vite.config.ts\nplugins: [\n    microtags({\n        cascade: true,\n        keep: ['my-notice'],\n    }),\n]\n```\n\n---\n\n### `microbuild`\n\nCLI for stripping `.render()` calls outside a bundler.\n\n```sh\n# stdin/stdout -- one file\ncat src/counter.ts | microbuild --cascade > dist/counter.ts\n\n# glob mode -- requires --outdir\nmicrobuild 'src/**/*.ts' --outdir dist --cascade --keep my-notice\n```\n\n`--keep` is repeatable and accepts comma-separated tag names. `--root`\nsets the base for output paths (defaults to the current directory).\nFiles are never rewritten in place.\n\nstdin mode transforms one file only. A multi-file app should use the\n[esbuild](#microtagsesbuild) or [vite](#microtagsvite) plugin, or\nglob mode.\n\n---\n\n### `client:true` vs `--keep`\n\nBoth prevent [`microbuild`](#microbuild) from stripping a component's\n`.render()` call, but they work at different levels:\n\n- **`{ client: true }`** is set in source, in the `.render()` options.\n  Use it for components that must render themselves in the browser --\n  for example, a notice inserted dynamically after page load. The\n  decision travels with the component and applies in every build.\n\n- **`--keep tag-name`** (or the `keep` option in the plugin) is set at\n  build time. Use it to override stripping for specific tags without\n  changing source, for example during development or in a build\n  variant that needs client rendering.\n\nBoth can be combined. A component is kept when either condition is met\n(union semantics).\n\n---\n\n## Differences from `nanotags`\n\n### Reactivity primitive\n\n`nanotags` uses `nanostores` atoms; `microtags` uses `alien-signals`.\n\n| nanotags (nanostores) | microtags (alien-signals) |\n|---|---|\n// Types and prop mapping shared by both builds of `microtags/preact`\n// (the default server build and the browser build). Never imports\n// render support. See ADR-010.\nimport type { FunctionComponent } from 'preact'\nimport type { RenderParts } from './builders.js'\n\n/**\n * The part of a microtags element class the adapter reads. Any class\n * from `setup` fits; `renderParts` is absent at runtime when the class\n * has no render link.\n */\nexport interface PreactElementClass<P = any> {\n    readonly TAG:string\n    readonly props:readonly string[]\n    readonly renderParts?:(\n        props:P,\n        options?:{ children?:string; attrs?:Record<string, string> }\n    ) => RenderParts\n}\n\n/** Map from callback prop name to DOM event name. */\nexport type EventMap = Record<string, string>\n\nexport interface ToPreactOptions<E extends EventMap = EventMap> {\n    /** e.g. `{ onChange: 'number-input:change' }` */\n    events?:E\n}\n\ntype AttrValue = string | number | boolean | null | undefined\n\n/** Host attributes passed through to the host tag. */\nexport interface PassthroughProps {\n    class?:string\n    id?:string\n    [aria:`aria-${string}`]:AttrValue\n    [data:`data-${string}`]:AttrValue\n}\n\n/** The declared props of an element class, all optional. */\nexport type DeclaredProps<C> =\n    C extends { renderParts?:(props:infer P, ...a:any[]) => any } ?\n        Partial<P> :\n        never\n\n/**\n * Props of the Preact component `toPreact` returns: the declared\n * props, one callback per mapped event, passthrough host attributes,\n * and no children.\n */\nexport type PreactProps<C, E extends EventMap = Record<never, never>> =\n    DeclaredProps<C> &\n    { [K in keyof E]?:(ev:CustomEvent) => void } &\n    PassthroughProps &\n    { children?:never }\n\nexport type PreactComponent<C, E extends EventMap> =\n    FunctionComponent<PreactProps<C, E>>\n\n/** Props split by where they go on the host. */\nexport interface SplitProps {\n    /** declared props, by name */\n    own:Record<string, unknown>\n    /** handlers, by DOM event name */\n    on:Record<string, unknown>\n    /** passthrough host attributes */\n    rest:Record<string, unknown>\n}\n\n/**\n * Split adapter props into declared props, event handlers (keyed by DOM\n * event name) and passthrough attributes. Throws, naming the tag, when\n * children are passed.\n */\nexport function splitProps (\n    El:PreactElementClass,\n    events:EventMap,\n    props:Record<string, unknown>\n):SplitProps {\n    if (props.children !== undefined) {\n        throw new Error(`microtags/preact: <${El.TAG}> takes no children`)\n    }\n    const own:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n    const on:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n    const rest:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n    for (const k in props) {\n        if (k === 'children') continue\n        if (El.props.includes(k)) own[k] = props[k]\n        else if (Object.hasOwn(events, k)) on[events[k]] = props[k]\n        else rest[k] = props[k]\n    }\n    return { own, on, rest }\n}\n// `microtags/preact`, browser build. Renders the host tag only: the\n// declared props go to the host's prop accessors, mapped events become\n// `on<event-name>` listeners, and a fixed empty `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`\n// keeps Preact out of the host's children. Never imports render\n// support. See ADR-010.\nimport { h, type VNode } from 'preact'\nimport {\n    splitProps,\n    type EventMap,\n    type PreactComponent,\n    type PreactElementClass,\n    type ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\nexport type {\n    DeclaredProps,\n    EventMap,\n    PassthroughProps,\n    PreactComponent,\n    PreactElementClass,\n    PreactProps,\n    ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\n// One shared value: Preact writes `innerHTML` only when `__html`\n// changes, and never while hydrating.\nconst EMPTY = { __html: '' }\n\n/**\n * Wrap a microtags element class as a Preact component. Preact owns the\n * host and its attributes; the element owns the host's children.\n */\nexport function toPreact<\n    C extends PreactElementClass,\n    E extends EventMap = Record<never, never>,\n> (El:C, options?:ToPreactOptions<E>):PreactComponent<C, E> {\n    const events:EventMap = options?.events ?? {}\n    return (props:Record<string, unknown>):VNode<any> => {\n        const { own, on, rest } = splitProps(El, events, props)\n        const vprops:Record<string, unknown> = { ...rest, ...own }\n        for (const k in on) vprops['on' + k] = on[k]\n        vprops.dangerouslySetInnerHTML = EMPTY\n        return h(El.TAG, vprops)\n    }\n}\n# ADR-010: Preact owns the host, the element owns its children\n\n**Date:** 2026-11-08\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size), [ADR-005][adr-005] and\n[ADR-009][adr-009] (render links and render support)\n\n## Context\n\n`../components` (`@substrate-system/components`) is moving its\ncomponents onto microtags, and they have to work inside Preact apps.\nThat covers a client-only Preact render and a Preact `hydrate` of a\nserver-rendered page. A microtags element placed in a Preact tree\nfails in both server cases.\n\nOn the server, Preact's `renderToString` emits an empty host, such as\n`<number-input min=\"1\"></number-input>`. Preact only knows the host\ntag. It does not know that the component has markup of its own, so\nthe page arrives without the component's input or buttons.\n\nIn the browser, Preact 10's `hydrate` collects every existing child of\nan element it hydrates and removes each child it has no vnode for. The\ncomponent's own markup has no vnode, so even if the server sent it,\n`hydrate` deletes it. The only exception is an element whose vnode has\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Preact leaves that element's children alone.\n\nThe terms below have their `CONTEXT.md` meanings. **Hydration** is the\nintent: attaching behaviour to markup that already exists in the\ndocument. **Adopt** is the mechanism: walking markup against existing\nDOM and binding to it without creating nodes. A microtags element\nhydrates itself when its class is registered. The adapter's job is to\nkeep Preact from undoing that hydration. It does not adopt anything\nitself.\n\n## Decision\n\nAdd a `microtags/preact` entry that exports `toPreact(El, options?)`.\nIt returns a Preact component that renders the element's host tag.\nOwnership is split at the host:\n\n- Preact owns the host tag and its attributes.\n- The element owns the host's children.\n\n**On the server**, the adapter builds the host vnode from the\ncomponent's render parts (the `renderParts` static, ADR-009's render\nsupport behind a new registry key). The attributes come from the\nparts' `attrs`, and the parts' `html` goes in through\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. `renderToString` then produces the same\nmarkup as the component's own `render` static. A class whose render\nlink was stripped has no `renderParts`, so the adapter throws an error\nthat names the tag.\n\n**In the browser**, the adapter gives the host one shared, fixed\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` whose `__html` is the empty string. It also\npasses the declared props as vnode props, which Preact assigns as\nproperties because the host defines an accessor for each one. Mapped\nevents are passed as `on<event-name>` props. The mechanism depends on\ntwo branches of Preact's element diff:\n\n1. While hydrating, Preact neither writes `innerHTML` nor removes the\n   element's existing children. The server markup stays and the\n   element adopts it.\n2. Outside hydration, Preact writes `innerHTML` only when the new\n   `__html` differs from the old one. The value never changes, so it\n   is written at most once, on the first non-hydrating render. On a\n   client-only mount that write empties the host once, and the element\n   renders itself when it connects. Later renders never touch the\n   children.\n\nBoth branches were verified in Preact 10.29.7. The `preact` dev\ndependency is pinned, so a Preact change arrives as a deliberate bump,\nand the browser tests (hydrate keeps inner nodes, re-render keeps\nthem, typed input survives) check it.\n\nThe browser build is selected by a `browser` export condition, as\n`microtags/htm` already is, and never imports render support.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\nADR-001-alien-signals-for-reactivity.md\nADR-002-no-shadow-dom.md\nADR-003-standard-schema-for-prop-validation.md\nADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\nADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\nADR-006-hono-html-scaffold.md\nADR-007-client-templater.md\nADR-008-serialized-server-state.md\nADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md\nADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md\nINDEX.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pv2gBRxELSJ2mp1pYW9ACq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
