{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MXEpBtRyGfhC2R4f4hWfwu","type":"tool_result","content":"// `microtags/preact`, default (Node and SSR) build. Renders the host\n// tag with its attributes and inner HTML from the component's render\n// parts, so `renderToString` matches the `render` static. Imports\n// render support, as the build transform does for a kept render link\n// (ADR-009). See ADR-010.\nimport { h, type VNode } from 'preact'\nimport './render-support.js'\nimport {\n    splitProps,\n    type EventMap,\n    type PreactComponent,\n    type PreactElementClass,\n    type ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\nexport type {\n    DeclaredProps,\n    EventMap,\n    PassthroughProps,\n    PreactComponent,\n    PreactElementClass,\n    PreactProps,\n    ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\n/**\n * Wrap a microtags element class as a Preact component. Preact owns the\n * host and its attributes; the element owns the host's children.\n */\nexport function toPreact<\n    C extends PreactElementClass,\n    E extends EventMap = Record<never, never>,\n> (El:C, options?:ToPreactOptions<E>):PreactComponent<C, E> {\n    const events:EventMap = options?.events ?? {}\n    return (props:Record<string, unknown>):VNode<any> => {\n        const { own, rest } = splitProps(El, events, props)\n        if (!El.renderParts) {\n            throw new Error(\n                `microtags/preact: <${El.TAG}> has no render link. On ` +\n                'the server, import the variant of this component that ' +\n                'keeps its render link.'\n            )\n        }\n        const extra:Record<string, string> = {}\n        for (const k in rest) {\n            if (rest[k] != null) extra[k] = String(rest[k])\n        }\n        const { tag, attrs, html } = El.renderParts(own, { attrs: extra })\n        const vprops:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n        for (const k in attrs) vprops[k] = attrs[k] === '' ? true : attrs[k]\n        vprops.dangerouslySetInnerHTML = { __html: html }\n        return h(tag, vprops)\n    }\n}\n800:options?)` which returns complete host markup, `renderParts(props,\n805:`renderParts` returns `{ tag, attrs, html }`: the host tag name, the\n817:const { tag, attrs, html }:RenderParts = MyCounter.renderParts({\n830:The static `render` (and `renderParts`) needs the server render\n835:Without it, `render` and `renderParts` throw an error naming that\n1493:component's static `render` and `renderParts` use. Import it for its\n1504:only code that calls a `render` or `renderParts` static without\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **A bare host tag.** No adapter, just `<number-input>` in JSX. The\n  server output is an empty host, and `hydrate` deletes whatever\n  server children the host had. This is the problem itself.\n- **A global `options.vnode` hook.** One hook that recognises every\n  microtags tag and injects its inner HTML. It is implicit: a page\n  changes behaviour depending on whether some module installed the\n  hook. It is global, so it affects every Preact tree in the page,\n  and it runs on every vnode, not only microtags hosts.\n- **A per-call `__html` that changes with props.** Render the inner\n  HTML from the current props on every render. When a prop changes,\n  the new `__html` differs from the old, so Preact writes `innerHTML`\n  over live DOM. That replaces the element's nodes and destroys their\n  state: bindings, focus, and values the visitor typed.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- The approach depends on two internal branches of Preact's diff, not\n  a documented contract. The pin and the browser tests turn a silent\n  break into a failing bump.\n- **Props before definition.** If the element is not yet defined when\n  Preact first assigns a prop, the property does not exist on the\n  element, so Preact sets an attribute instead. The adapter does not\n  work around this. A component's declared props already read their\n  attribute at connect time, so the value still arrives. This ADR\n  records it as a known edge.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- No Preact children. The adapter does not accept them: passing them is\n  a type error, and the adapter throws in development. Slotting vnodes\n  into element-owned markup is out of scope.\n- The browser build of `microtags/preact` carries no render code. It\n  does not import render support, so with every render link stripped\n  a client bundle stays as small as ADR-004 requires.\n- `preact` is an optional peer dependency, like `typescript`. Core and\n  every entry other than `microtags/preact` never import it.\n- Render support gains a second registered function, the parts\n  function, under `Symbol.for('microtags.renderParts')`. ADR-009's\n  render record contract is unchanged, so any copy of core keeps\n  working with any copy of render support.\n\nNo ADR is superseded.\n\n[adr-004]: ./ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\n[adr-005]: ./ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\n[adr-009]: ./ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd578c50-847c-417e-9dc9-883d9c7ecbfc","uuid":"28a93b50-1080-4714-bf8c-561a4acd8816","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:22:08.781Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// `microtags/preact`, default (Node and SSR) build. Renders the host\n// tag with its attributes and inner HTML from the component's render\n// parts, so `renderToString` matches the `render` static. Imports\n// render support, as the build transform does for a kept render link\n// (ADR-009). See ADR-010.\nimport { h, type VNode } from 'preact'\nimport './render-support.js'\nimport {\n    splitProps,\n    type EventMap,\n    type PreactComponent,\n    type PreactElementClass,\n    type ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\nexport type {\n    DeclaredProps,\n    EventMap,\n    PassthroughProps,\n    PreactComponent,\n    PreactElementClass,\n    PreactProps,\n    ToPreactOptions,\n} from './preact-shared.js'\n\n/**\n * Wrap a microtags element class as a Preact component. Preact owns the\n * host and its attributes; the element owns the host's children.\n */\nexport function toPreact<\n    C extends PreactElementClass,\n    E extends EventMap = Record<never, never>,\n> (El:C, options?:ToPreactOptions<E>):PreactComponent<C, E> {\n    const events:EventMap = options?.events ?? {}\n    return (props:Record<string, unknown>):VNode<any> => {\n        const { own, rest } = splitProps(El, events, props)\n        if (!El.renderParts) {\n            throw new Error(\n                `microtags/preact: <${El.TAG}> has no render link. On ` +\n                'the server, import the variant of this component that ' +\n                'keeps its render link.'\n            )\n        }\n        const extra:Record<string, string> = {}\n        for (const k in rest) {\n            if (rest[k] != null) extra[k] = String(rest[k])\n        }\n        const { tag, attrs, html } = El.renderParts(own, { attrs: extra })\n        const vprops:Record<string, unknown> = {}\n        for (const k in attrs) vprops[k] = attrs[k] === '' ? true : attrs[k]\n        vprops.dangerouslySetInnerHTML = { __html: html }\n        return h(tag, vprops)\n    }\n}\n800:options?)` which returns complete host markup, `renderParts(props,\n805:`renderParts` returns `{ tag, attrs, html }`: the host tag name, the\n817:const { tag, attrs, html }:RenderParts = MyCounter.renderParts({\n830:The static `render` (and `renderParts`) needs the server render\n835:Without it, `render` and `renderParts` throw an error naming that\n1493:component's static `render` and `renderParts` use. Import it for its\n1504:only code that calls a `render` or `renderParts` static without\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **A bare host tag.** No adapter, just `<number-input>` in JSX. The\n  server output is an empty host, and `hydrate` deletes whatever\n  server children the host had. This is the problem itself.\n- **A global `options.vnode` hook.** One hook that recognises every\n  microtags tag and injects its inner HTML. It is implicit: a page\n  changes behaviour depending on whether some module installed the\n  hook. It is global, so it affects every Preact tree in the page,\n  and it runs on every vnode, not only microtags hosts.\n- **A per-call `__html` that changes with props.** Render the inner\n  HTML from the current props on every render. When a prop changes,\n  the new `__html` differs from the old, so Preact writes `innerHTML`\n  over live DOM. That replaces the element's nodes and destroys their\n  state: bindings, focus, and values the visitor typed.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- The approach depends on two internal branches of Preact's diff, not\n  a documented contract. The pin and the browser tests turn a silent\n  break into a failing bump.\n- **Props before definition.** If the element is not yet defined when\n  Preact first assigns a prop, the property does not exist on the\n  element, so Preact sets an attribute instead. The adapter does not\n  work around this. A component's declared props already read their\n  attribute at connect time, so the value still arrives. This ADR\n  records it as a known edge.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- No Preact children. The adapter does not accept them: passing them is\n  a type error, and the adapter throws in development. Slotting vnodes\n  into element-owned markup is out of scope.\n- The browser build of `microtags/preact` carries no render code. It\n  does not import render support, so with every render link stripped\n  a client bundle stays as small as ADR-004 requires.\n- `preact` is an optional peer dependency, like `typescript`. Core and\n  every entry other than `microtags/preact` never import it.\n- Render support gains a second registered function, the parts\n  function, under `Symbol.for('microtags.renderParts')`. ADR-009's\n  render record contract is unchanged, so any copy of core keeps\n  working with any copy of render support.\n\nNo ADR is superseded.\n\n[adr-004]: ./ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\n[adr-005]: ./ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\n[adr-009]: ./ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MXEpBtRyGfhC2R4f4hWfwu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
